{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And she shall remove the garment of her captivity.</b> Because she served idolatry in them, as in והחליפו שמלותיכם, and whatever can be removed from her of all that she had on her while she was still a Canaanitess, you remove, such as her hair and her nails." "<b>Garment of her captivity.</b> And there is no need for her to wash, since it was already stated אתם ושביכם." "<b>And she shall weep.</b> For weeping clears the mind and makes one forget the distress." "<b>Et her father and et her mother.</b> For she thinks perhaps they were killed when she was taken captive." "<b>And afterward you may come to her.</b> But not before, for it is not the way of the world that she should weep while you play with her."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:38.805441876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}